ble ≈ (P−1)/(M+P−1)-type expressions) is expected as an internal sanity control. This validates the simulator's structure, not the hypothesis.\n\nImportant: the deliverable is the final experiment design document (rationale, controls, analysis plan, feasibility), not an executed experiment. You may include pseudocode for the schedule generators and simulator; do not run or claim to run anything. Also state expected outcomes as hypotheses with the reasoning behind them (1F1B/1F1B-I/ZB-1p throughput rising toward asymptote with M; ZB-2p already near-peak at small M), explicitly framed as predictions to be tested, not findings.", "required_handoff_stage": "result", "approach_approved": true}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null, "reasoning_content": null, "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "critic_result": null, "kind": "MessageEvent"}
